<heading>su - Substitute user / login.</heading>

<rule/>

<heading level="2">
Usage
</heading>

<pre>
  su USER
  su USER --password SECRET
  su USER --password SECRET --administrative
  su USER --password SECRET --temporary
</pre>

<heading level="2">
Description
</heading>

<paragraph>
Logs in as the specified user. If the password is not provided
and the system requires one, an interactive form is displayed
to enter it.
</paragraph>

<paragraph>
On success, the session identity is set to the new user and
all permission checks use that identity from that point on.
</paragraph>

<heading level="2">
Examples
</heading>

<pre>
su root
  Log in as root. If a password is required,
  an interactive form will appear.

su stefan --password 123
  Log in as stefan with the given password.

su stefan --password 123 --administrative
  Log in and establish an administrative security context.
  The password is the conscious confirmation of that context.

su stefan --password 123 --temporary
  Log in with a temporary context that elevates exactly one
  invocation and falls back to normal afterwards.
</pre>

<heading level="2">
See also
</heading>

<paragraph>
whoami
</paragraph>
